  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, resnet50, transformer, concat) achieved 47.1% accuracy at a high cost of 9.06 GPU hours, with the transformer aggregation likely being the dominant cost driver. Uncertainty: it is unclear whether the transformer aggregation is meaningfully contributing to performance or whether a simpler avgpool aggregation would yield comparable accuracy at a fraction of the cost. This experiment (config_002) is a clean single-variable ablation—changing only aggregation from transformer to avgpool while keeping all other settings identical—so any accuracy difference can be attributed to the aggregation method. If avgpool performs similarly (~47%), we can eliminate transformer-based configs from the search, saving substantial GPU hours across the remaining 8 experiments and redirecting budget toward exploring other dimensions (RNA encoder, image encoder, profile setting). If transformer is clearly superior, we retain it for future experiments. Expected relative cost: significantly lower than config_001 (estimated ~4–5 GPU hours vs 9.06), since avgpool replaces the compute-heavy transformer layer. This is the best use of experiment 2 because it directly reduces uncertainty about the most expensive architectural component with a minimal, interpretable change, and the cost savings (or confirmation) will shape the strategy for all remaining experiments."
}

